From: Tristan Stiller <stillertristan77@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 22:51:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DVDVideoCodecAmlogic: reset DoVi start decode state on seek

Amlogic DoVi streams can stall after seeking when the bitstream converter
continues with stale start-decode state. The hardware decoder may never
resume feeding frames, leaving playback stuck with a nearly full amstream
buffer and invalid audio PTS.

Handle Dolby Vision streams like H.264 on codec reset: keep the converter's
RPU/SPS/PPS metadata cache intact, but require a fresh decode start after
the discontinuity. This fixes FEL seek stalls without clearing the converter
state needed for dual-layer DoVi playback.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
index a4a7dc28a3..11be9b7f4a 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecAmlogic.cpp
@@ -688,8 +688,12 @@ void CDVDVideoCodecAmlogic::Reset(void)
 
   m_mpeg2_sequence_pts = 0;
   m_has_keyframe = false;
-  if (m_bitstream && m_hints.codec == AV_CODEC_ID_H264)
-    m_bitstream->ResetStartDecode();
+  if (m_bitstream &&
+      (m_hints.codec == AV_CODEC_ID_H264 ||
+       m_hints.hdrType == StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION ||
+       m_hints.dovi_el_type == DOVIELType::TYPE_FEL ||
+       m_hints.dovi_el_type == DOVIELType::TYPE_MEL))
+    m_bitstream->ResetStartDecode();
 }
 
 CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn CDVDVideoCodecAmlogic::GetPicture(VideoPicture* pVideoPicture)
